WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.180
Emperor Wu received Zhang Qian in the Chang'an palace, personally handed him the envoy's staff, and ordered him to go on a mission to the Western Regions.

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:14.400
Zhang Qian led a camel caravan into the boundless desert, beginning the long journey.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:22.380
On the way, Xiongnu cavalry suddenly appeared and detained Zhang Qian's whole party.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:31.120
In the Xiongnu camp, Zhang Qian always gripped the Han staff tightly and would never bow his head — and the wait lasted many years.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.880
Later he seized a chance to escape, crossing mountains and ridges, and continued west.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:43.000
He met the Dayuezhi people, spoke warmly with them, and recorded much of what he saw and heard in the Western Regions.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:50.680
Back in Chang'an, Zhang Qian reported all he had seen to Emperor Wu, opening the great door to the Western Regions.

